# skript-combat

Skript-minestom addon. Vendored combat library is `io.github.togar2.pvp` (MinestomPvP). Addon code is `com.github.hapily04.skriptcombat`. Prefer changing the addon, not the library.

## Enablement

- `MinestomPvP.init(false, true)` and `CombatPlayerImpl` as player provider stay **global** (registries, keep-alive, jump-from-move).
- Do **not** `addChild(MinestomPvP.events())` on the global handler. Combat listeners are an `EventNode<EntityInstanceEvent>` attached to `instance.eventNode()`.
- `CombatInstanceBinder` owns attach/detach, explosion supplier restore, and the config currently set on an instance.
- Jump physics still run everywhere because every player is `CombatPlayerImpl`. Attack/damage/food/projectiles only run on instances with a bound config.

## Skript

- Minestom `Instance` type code name is `instance` (`%instances%`), not `world`.
- No `config.yml`. Scripts opt instances in.
- Configs are a **SectionExpression** (`ExprCombatConfiguration`): `[a] [new] combat configuration`, `[a] modern vanilla combat configuration`, `[a] legacy vanilla combat configuration`. Optional boolean entries per feature (`vanilla attack: false`). Omitted keys keep the preset. Version is the pattern, not a `version:` entry. Only one knockback feature may be `true` (they share `FeatureType.KNOCKBACK`).
- Feature keys live in `CombatFeatureCatalog`. Empty preset uses `CombatFeatures.empty()` + modern version; vanilla presets use `getVanilla(...)`, not the `modernVanilla()` singleton.
- Bind with property `combat config[uration] of %instances%` (`ExprCombatConfigOfInstance`): **set** applies, **delete/reset** unbinds. Do not add apply/disable effects.
- `combat is enabled (in|on|for) %instances%` checks the binder.
- Elements load from `com.github.hapily04.skriptcombat.elements` (and subpackages). Compile against `skript-minestom` (`%instances%`, `SectionExpression`, `EntryValidator` / `LiteralEntryData`).
